// An else-less `if` used as a VALUE in ARGUMENT position. `vl check` returns 0 and the
// emitter refuses with `emitProgram: union atom has no value box` — clause 2. The join
// `i32 | null` exists only as an inference, and the per-rep value boxes are minted at union
// REGISTRATION, so there is no box for the `i32` arm to coerce into (D1745).
//
// The row this probe used to witness was `emitProgram: if-expression requires an else arm`,
// and no spelling reaches that literal any more: of fourteen else-less delivery positions —
// binding, annotated binding, return, inferred return, user-function argument, hole
// parameter, struct field, map value, list element, and the boolean/f64/string arm sets —
// ten RUN and the rest refuse or miscompile for the reasons above.
// Should print 1.
print(if true { 1 })
